                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "64bd9f24-0f1e-3df0-b0bc-e64ff77f72e6",
                        "entry_id": "ef34a14e-cee1-3f5d-8a6a-db90a994de9b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To drive or remove (bees) from a hive."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "51e2daab-842f-4826-b3e0-eaa69d6ead33",
                                "sense_id": "64bd9f24-0f1e-3df0-b0bc-e64ff77f72e6",
                                "text": "[T]he Mercers encreaſing prodigiouſly vvent back into the City; there like Bees unhiv'd they hover about a vvhile, not knovving vvhere to fix; but at laſt, as if they vvould come back to the old Hive in Pater-noſter Rovv, but could not be admitted, the ſvvarm ſettled on Lu[d]gate-hill."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8a67abdb-2f3b-44b3-bfb7-d67c28839d7c",
                                "sense_id": "64bd9f24-0f1e-3df0-b0bc-e64ff77f72e6",
                                "text": "and unhived those numerous swarms of labouring bees which used to drop honey-dews over all this kingdom, to place in their room swarms of senseless drones."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "116fc02e-ce80-44f9-b82e-700e860d04a3",
                                "sense_id": "64bd9f24-0f1e-3df0-b0bc-e64ff77f72e6",
                                "text": "His broad hands smoothed her head, as fain to brush it free From fancies, swarms that stung like bees unhived."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5a6e60fc-d45f-3296-b0ce-2c07f84ef973",
                        "entry_id": "ef34a14e-cee1-3f5d-8a6a-db90a994de9b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To expel (a crowd, etc.) of habitation or shelter; to disband."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "archaic",
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "db2510cb-c24d-47d9-b305-9f8256c9503f",
                                "sense_id": "5a6e60fc-d45f-3296-b0ce-2c07f84ef973",
                                "text": "But if there be any who are herin delinquent; it were more justice and generosity to give a Catalogue of such Drones to those who have an undoubted Power to make them Labour, or Unhive them: And that the Righteous be not as the Wicked."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6f5bc6d4-8e3f-4510-96d6-2284a2b9db80",
                                "sense_id": "5a6e60fc-d45f-3296-b0ce-2c07f84ef973",
                                "text": "We need no more, one age will discover the effects; the people insensibly file northwards, where they intrench themselves in the mud; the ocean is debarred her wantering, the hollow land made frim, the lakes drained; the loose sand becomes a stable foundation for great emporiums; the ancient cities of Flanders, Brabant, and Arois unhive themselves into the new ones of Holland, Zealand, and West Friesland; and, in a word, the younger colonies (notwithstanding the disadvantages of nature) yielding an asylum to liberty, shall equal and far exceed what the former ever were."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe641574-4b59-4b50-aa3f-587d367970c3",
                                "sense_id": "5a6e60fc-d45f-3296-b0ce-2c07f84ef973",
                                "text": "We conquering Ensigns to Rome might extend, If each man was faithful and true to his friend; There to unhive the old Pope and his Crew, And lead them in Triumph New London to view :"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bb0a20ec-f314-4c71-a4d4-63c6a6d58474",
                                "sense_id": "5a6e60fc-d45f-3296-b0ce-2c07f84ef973",
                                "text": "Here Harlotry unhives her swarms Of puffed and painted faces, Parading their half-faded charms With meretricious graces."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "d0feb0c1-622b-3bcd-944b-3d71376604dc",
                        "entry_id": "ef34a14e-cee1-3f5d-8a6a-db90a994de9b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To break apart; to disrupt."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "24844498-239f-42b5-ae30-f3ad5b3aa5e2",
                                "sense_id": "d0feb0c1-622b-3bcd-944b-3d71376604dc",
                                "text": "It would have been a continual hell of time-consuming impugnable argument, bringing on the kind of conjugal weather that closesup the rose and unhives the family for lack of any honey whatsoever."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "54a64bbf-2cbd-4524-974f-8855d95b6513",
                                "sense_id": "d0feb0c1-622b-3bcd-944b-3d71376604dc",
                                "text": "You can't unsocialize your self, and you can't unhive yourself. We are merely a goal-less hive, a hive without purpose other than sustenance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e115d9a5-270b-4f88-9662-5c1ebde988bd",
                                "sense_id": "d0feb0c1-622b-3bcd-944b-3d71376604dc",
                                "text": "The Russian general staff is said to have a hive mind. \"Unhive” it by sowing uncertainty, causing its officers to make bad decisions that can be exploited."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
